fix: resolve Aspire AppHost endpoint naming conflict

FIXES:
- Unique endpoint names for each microservice (was causing "Endpoint with name 'http' already exists" error)
- Correct path resolution from AppHost binary location to project root
- Each service now has distinct endpoint identifier (gateway-http, user-http, etc.)

DETAILS:
- AppContext.BaseDirectory resolves to app/server/AppHost/bin/Debug/net9.0
- Navigate up 4 levels to reach app/server root directory
- Fixed path calculation for project discovery during initialization

TESTING:
- Solution builds successfully (0 errors, 4 warnings about unused packages)
- Docker infrastructure services running (postgres, keycloak, redis, rabbitmq)
- Services can start individually without Aspire orchestration
- Added helper scripts for local development and testing

INFRASTRUCTURE ADDED:
- docker-compose.services.yml: Complete microservices deployment configuration
- Dockerfile.Base: Base Docker image for building all services
- run-services.ps1: PowerShell script to start all services locally
- test-apis.ps1: Test script to verify service health and connectivity
- HOW_TO_RUN.md: Comprehensive documentation for running the system

DEPLOYMENT OPTIONS:
1. Local development: .\run-services.ps1 (starts services in separate terminals)
2. Docker: docker-compose -f docker-compose.services.yml up
3. Individual services: dotnet run from each project directory

